      "category": "etymology",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The first Hungarian railway line, opened in 1846, ran through Rákospalota, turning the forested area into a leisure spot with restaurants.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        15
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/R%C3%A1kospalota",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Between August and November 1919 a Romanian garrison occupied Rákospalota during the War of 1918‑1919.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        8
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/R%C3%A1kospalota",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "The old Catholic chapel beside the Szilas brook, built in 1735, is one of four national monuments listed for Rákospalota.",
